{
  "transcript": "The fourth reason is that I'm busy is genuinely useful. It is a shield. Sometimes it means I cannot take on more. Sometimes it means I do not want to make this decision. Sometimes it means please stop asking me questions. And sometimes it means I have no idea what I am doing, but I need to look calm until the answer shows up. This is not always dishonest. A lot of people really are overloaded. The shield is real. The problem is that busy slowly becomes the only acceptable way to say no. You cannot always say I need quiet time to think.\" That sounds suspiciously relaxed. You cannot always say, \"This meeting could have been a message.\" That sounds dangerous. So people just say, \"I'm busy,\" and everyone nods. Because everyone else is also busy or pretending or both.",
